  "adaptations": [
    "Relative includes use the existing layout/deswizzle modules.",
    "Dirty tracking registers one process-lifetime checked callback pair through the host-owned bridge.",
    "Dirty page ownership and actual protection are checked before handling stale faults.",
    "Dirty allocation, prepare and retirement failures are returned; no private crash handler is installed.",
    "Single translation-unit modules.inc isolates private names without changing public entry points.",
    "Checked ownership and certificate publication return allocation failures instead of abort; hash-table growth is transactional.",
    "Quiescent reset APIs are restricted to whole-context teardown after all users and GPU work have drained.",
    "Upstream synthetic tests adapt private host hooks to a test-only callback pair; original assertion bodies are retained.",
    "Kernel permission queries for writable NONE pages own the canonical BUSY state, preventing a full protect/unprotect ABA race from rejecting legal writes."
  ]
